# Recommended cron entry for the pm-edge parquet compaction job.
#
# The forward indexer and resolution watcher write one small parquet part-file
# per partition per flush (~every 15 s). Left unchecked, each (table, venue,
# date) directory accumulates thousands of tiny files, which makes recursive
# read_parquet('.../**/*.parquet') globs hang and slows ext4 lookups and rsync.
#
# This job merges those small part-files into a few large ones for every
# partition strictly older than today (UTC). It never touches today's partition,
# so it is safe to run while the indexer is live, and it verifies row counts
# before deleting any source file.
#
# Roll out in two phases:
#
# 1. Dry-run only for a few days (logs what *would* be compacted, writes nothing):
#
# 30 9 * * * /opt/pm-edge/.venv/bin/python /opt/pm-edge/scripts/compact_parquet.py --dry-run >> /opt/pm-edge/data/compact_parquet.log 2>&1
#
# 2. Once the dry-run output looks right, enable the real compaction. Schedule it
#    at a low-activity hour and BEFORE the laptop's morning rsync so the smaller
#    file set is what gets pulled:
#
# 30 9 * * * /opt/pm-edge/.venv/bin/python /opt/pm-edge/scripts/compact_parquet.py >> /opt/pm-edge/data/compact_parquet.log 2>&1
#
# By default it compacts both configured archive roots
# (PM_EDGE_FORWARD_INDEXER_OUTPUT_DIR and the resolution watcher output dir).
# Pass --root PATH (repeatable) to target specific roots, and --target-file-mb
# to change the ~256 MiB per-file cap.
